{"uid":"modules/lazy_commander.py","name":"lazy_commander.py","qualname":"modules/lazy_commander.py","kind":"module","file":"modules/lazy_commander.py","line":1,"end_line":365,"language":"py","signature":"","params":[],"returns":"","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"Fleet commander: allocate the next work slice across loop tasks.","description":"Mined from sapper-v2's field commander and reimplemented LazyOwn-native.\nWhen several loop tasks are alive at once, a slot-clock loop reads the\nmulti-task board, asks one LLM pass which task gets the next slice\n(``work``, ``hire``, ``fire`` or ``stop``) and falls back to\nleast-worked-first fairness when the model is unavailable or answers\nnonsense. This is the operator-side coordination layer (keep the agent\nfleet alive and productive); victim-side beaconing stays in ``lazyc2``.\n\nOne contract per file (SOLID): decision parsing, board rendering, prompt\nfencing and the allocation loop live here. Engine I/O is injected so\n``modules.lazy_loop`` stays the only orchestrator and no import cycle\nappears:\n\n- ``board_fn`` -> the task board (engine ``list_tasks``).\n- ``complete_fn`` -> ``(prompt, max_tokens) -> reply`` (``LlmPool``).\n- ``work_fn`` -> ``(task_id, workers) -> run result`` (engine ``run``).\n- ``pause_fn`` -> ``(task_id, reason) -> bool`` (engine ``pause_task``).\n\nThe commander never edits tasks, goals or scope: it only spends slices\nand pauses stalled work, exactly the levers an operator has by hand.","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"","members":["modules/lazy_commander.py::COMMANDER_ACTIONS","modules/lazy_commander.py::DEFAULT_COMMANDER_MINUTES","modules/lazy_commander.py::DEFAULT_COMMANDER_SLICES","modules/lazy_commander.py::DEFAULT_COMMANDER_WORKERS","modules/lazy_commander.py::COMMANDER_HIRE_WORKERS","modules/lazy_commander.py::COMMANDER_NOOP_LIMIT","modules/lazy_commander.py::CommanderDecision","modules/lazy_commander.py::parse_commander_decision","modules/lazy_commander.py::render_board","modules/lazy_commander.py::build_commander_prompt","modules/lazy_commander.py::format_commander_budget","modules/lazy_commander.py::LazyCommander"],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
